ocol)</strong></h1>
<h2 data-start=3D"88" data-end=3D"109" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"91"=
 data-end=3D"107">Introduction</strong></h2>
<p data-start=3D"110" data-end=3D"366" class=3D"">Le protocole <strong data=
-start=3D"123" data-end=3D"160">ARP (Address Resolution Protocol)</strong> =
joue un r=C3=B4le fondamental dans le fonctionnement des r=C3=A9seaux sous =
Windows. Il permet de <strong data-start=3D"248" data-end=3D"291">convertir=
 une adresse IP en adresse MAC</strong> afin que les appareils d'un r=C3=A9=
seau local puissent communiquer entre eux.</p>
<p data-start=3D"368" data-end=3D"711" class=3D"">Dans ce tutoriel, nous al=
lons explorer en profondeur :<br data-start=3D"422" data-end=3D"425">
=E2=9C=85 <strong data-start=3D"427" data-end=3D"465">Le fonctionnement du =
protocole ARP</strong><br data-start=3D"465" data-end=3D"468">
=E2=9C=85 <strong data-start=3D"470" data-end=3D"532">Les types de messages=
 ARP (Request, Reply, Gratuitous ARP)</strong><br data-start=3D"532" data-e=
nd=3D"535">
=E2=9C=85 <strong data-start=3D"537" data-end=3D"580">Le cache ARP sous Win=
dows et sa gestion</strong><br data-start=3D"580" data-end=3D"583">
=E2=9C=85 <strong data-start=3D"585" data-end=3D"653">Les vuln=C3=A9rabilit=
=C3=A9s et attaques ARP (Spoofing, Man-in-the-Middle)</strong><br data-star=
t=3D"653" data-end=3D"656">
=E2=9C=85 <strong data-start=3D"658" data-end=3D"709">Les outils Windows po=
ur surveiller et g=C3=A9rer ARP</strong></p>
<hr data-start=3D"713" data-end=3D"716" class=3D"">
<h2 data-start=3D"718" data-end=3D"762" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"72=
1" data-end=3D"760">1. Qu=E2=80=99est-ce que le Protocole ARP ?</strong></h=
2>
<p data-start=3D"764" data-end=3D"958" class=3D"">Le <strong data-start=3D"=
767" data-end=3D"784">protocole ARP</strong> est un protocole de la couche =
<strong data-start=3D"815" data-end=3D"862">Liaison de donn=C3=A9es (couche=
 2 du mod=C3=A8le OSI)</strong> qui permet de trouver <strong data-start=3D=
"885" data-end=3D"928">l=E2=80=99adresse MAC associ=C3=A9e =C3=A0 une adres=
se IP</strong> dans un r=C3=A9seau local (LAN).</p>
<p data-start=3D"960" data-end=3D"1001" class=3D"">=F0=9F=93=8C <strong dat=
a-start=3D"963" data-end=3D"999">Pourquoi ARP est-il n=C3=A9cessaire ?</str=
ong></p>
<ul data-start=3D"1002" data-end=3D"1294">
<li data-start=3D"1002" data-end=3D"1086" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"1004" data-end=3D"1086" class=3D"">Lorsqu=E2=80=99un appar=
eil veut communiquer via IP, il doit envoyer des trames Ethernet.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1087" data-end=3D"1155" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"1089" data-end=3D"1155" class=3D"">Chaque trame Ethernet c=
ontient <strong data-start=3D"1120" data-end=3D"1152">l=E2=80=99adresse MAC=
 de destination</strong>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1156" data-end=3D"1225" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"1158" data-end=3D"1225" class=3D"">Or, l=E2=80=99exp=C3=A9=
diteur <strong data-start=3D"1175" data-end=3D"1206">ne conna=C3=AEt que l=
=E2=80=99adresse IP</strong> du destinataire.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1226" data-end=3D"1294" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"1228" data-end=3D"1294" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"1=
228" data-end=3D"1292">ARP est utilis=C3=A9 pour r=C3=A9cup=C3=A9rer l=E2=
=80=99adresse MAC correspondante.</strong></p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"1296" data-end=3D"1299" class=3D"">
<h2 data-start=3D"1301" data-end=3D"1344" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
1304" data-end=3D"1342">2. Fonctionnement du Protocole ARP</strong></h2>
<h3 data-start=3D"1346" data-end=3D"1374" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
1350" data-end=3D"1372">2.1. Processus ARP</strong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"1376" data-end=3D"1442" class=3D"">1=EF=B8=8F=E2=83=A3 <st=
rong data-start=3D"1380" data-end=3D"1440">Un appareil veut envoyer des don=
n=C3=A9es sur le r=C3=A9seau local</strong></p>
<ul data-start=3D"1446" data-end=3D"2072">
<li data-start=3D"1446" data-end=3D"1575" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"1448" data-end=3D"1575" class=3D"">Ex : Un PC Windows (<co=
de data-start=3D"1468" data-end=3D"1482">192.168.1.10</code>) veut communiq=
uer avec une imprimante (<code data-start=3D"1522" data-end=3D"1536">192.16=
8.1.20</code>).<br data-start=3D"1538" data-end=3D"1541">
2=EF=B8=8F=E2=83=A3 <strong data-start=3D"1545" data-end=3D"1573">Il v=C3=
=A9rifie son cache ARP</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1579" data-end=3D"1740" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"1581" data-end=3D"1740" class=3D"">Si l=E2=80=99adresse MA=
C de <code data-start=3D"1601" data-end=3D"1615">192.168.1.20</code> est d=
=C3=A9j=C3=A0 dans le cache ARP, il l=E2=80=99utilise directement.<br data-=
start=3D"1669" data-end=3D"1672">
3=EF=B8=8F=E2=83=A3 <strong data-start=3D"1676" data-end=3D"1738">Si l=E2=
=80=99adresse MAC n=E2=80=99est pas trouv=C3=A9e, ARP envoie une requ=C3=AA=
te</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1744" data-end=3D"1885" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"1746" data-end=3D"1885" class=3D"">Une <strong data-start=
=3D"1750" data-end=3D"1765">ARP Request</strong> est envoy=C3=A9e sous form=
e de <strong data-start=3D"1792" data-end=3D"1805">broadcast</strong> (<cod=
e data-start=3D"1807" data-end=3D"1826">FF:FF:FF:FF:FF:FF</code>).<br data-=
start=3D"1828" data-end=3D"1831">
4=EF=B8=8F=E2=83=A3 <strong data-start=3D"1835" data-end=3D"1883">L=E2=80=
=99appareil cible r=C3=A9pond avec son adresse MAC</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1889" data-end=3D"1990" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"1891" data-end=3D"1990" class=3D"">L=E2=80=99imprimante en=
voie une <strong data-start=3D"1915" data-end=3D"1928">ARP Reply</strong> a=
vec son adresse MAC.<br data-start=3D"1950" data-end=3D"1953">
5=EF=B8=8F=E2=83=A3 <strong data-start=3D"1957" data-end=3D"1988">Le cache =
ARP est mis =C3=A0 jour</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1994" data-end=3D"2072" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"1996" data-end=3D"2072" class=3D"">L=E2=80=99adresse MAC d=
e l=E2=80=99imprimante est stock=C3=A9e pour les futures communications.</p=
>
</li>
</ul>
