olution de Noms</strong></h1>
<h2 data-start=3D"87" data-end=3D"106" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"90"=
 data-end=3D"106">Introduction</strong></h2>
<p data-start=3D"108" data-end=3D"535" class=3D"">Le <strong data-start=3D"=
111" data-end=3D"118">DNS</strong> (Domain Name System) est un service fond=
amental dans tout r=C3=A9seau informatique, y compris les r=C3=A9seaux loca=
ux sous Windows. Il permet de traduire des noms de domaine (comme <strong d=
ata-start=3D"290" data-end=3D"309"><a data-start=3D"292" data-end=3D"307" r=
el=3D"noopener" target=3D"_new" class=3D"" href=3D"http://www.example.com/"=
>www.example.com</a></strong>) en adresses IP num=C3=A9riques que les ordin=
ateurs peuvent comprendre. Cette fonctionnalit=C3=A9 est cruciale pour le b=
on fonctionnement d=E2=80=99un r=C3=A9seau local, notamment pour la navigat=
ion web, l=E2=80=99acc=C3=A8s aux services r=C3=A9seau, et plus encore.</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"537" data-end=3D"568" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"54=
1" data-end=3D"566">Objectifs du tutoriel</strong> :</h3>
<ul data-start=3D"569" data-end=3D"791">
<li data-start=3D"569" data-end=3D"616" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"571" data-end=3D"616" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"571=
" data-end=3D"585">Comprendre</strong> le r=C3=B4le du DNS dans un r=C3=A9s=
eau.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"617" data-end=3D"709" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"619" data-end=3D"709" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"619=
" data-end=3D"633">Configurer</strong> un serveur DNS local ou utiliser un =
serveur DNS externe (comme Google DNS).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"710" data-end=3D"791" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"712" data-end=3D"791" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"712=
" data-end=3D"724">D=C3=A9panner</strong> les probl=C3=A8mes courants li=C3=
=A9s =C3=A0 la r=C3=A9solution des noms sous Windows.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"793" data-end=3D"796" class=3D"">
<h2 data-start=3D"798" data-end=3D"830" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"80=
1" data-end=3D"830">1. Qu=E2=80=99est-ce que le DNS ?</strong></h2>
<p data-start=3D"832" data-end=3D"1126" class=3D"">Le <strong data-start=3D=
"835" data-end=3D"863">DNS (Domain Name System)</strong> est un syst=C3=A8m=
e de traduction qui permet de convertir des noms d=E2=80=99h=C3=B4tes (nom =
de domaine) en adresses IP. Cela est n=C3=A9cessaire car les ordinateurs et=
 les appareils connect=C3=A9s =C3=A0 Internet ou =C3=A0 un r=C3=A9seau util=
isent des adresses IP pour localiser et communiquer entre eux.</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"1128" data-end=3D"1164" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
1132" data-end=3D"1162">1.1. Fonctionnement du DNS</strong></h3>
<ol data-start=3D"1165" data-end=3D"1590">
<li data-start=3D"1165" data-end=3D"1331" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"1168" data-end=3D"1331" class=3D"">Lorsqu=E2=80=99un appar=
eil envoie une requ=C3=AAte pour un nom de domaine (par exemple, <strong da=
ta-start=3D"1243" data-end=3D"1262"><a data-start=3D"1245" data-end=3D"1260=
" rel=3D"noopener" target=3D"_new" class=3D"" href=3D"http://www.example.co=
m/">www.example.com</a></strong>), il consulte un <strong data-start=3D"128=
0" data-end=3D"1295">serveur DNS</strong> pour obtenir l'adresse IP associ=
=C3=A9e.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1332" data-end=3D"1492" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"1335" data-end=3D"1492" class=3D"">Si le serveur DNS local=
 ne poss=C3=A8de pas l=E2=80=99adresse IP demand=C3=A9e, il enverra la requ=
=C3=AAte =C3=A0 un serveur DNS sup=C3=A9rieur, et ainsi de suite jusqu=E2=
=80=99=C3=A0 obtenir la r=C3=A9ponse.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1493" data-end=3D"1590" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"1496" data-end=3D"1590" class=3D"">Une fois l'adresse IP o=
btenue, l'appareil peut =C3=A9tablir une connexion au serveur correspondant=
.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<h3 data-start=3D"1592" data-end=3D"1631" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
1596" data-end=3D"1631">1.2. Pourquoi utiliser le DNS ?</strong></h3>
<ul data-start=3D"1632" data-end=3D"1946">
<li data-start=3D"1632" data-end=3D"1726" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"1634" data-end=3D"1726" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"1=
634" data-end=3D"1652">Simplification</strong> : Il est plus facile de se s=
ouvenir de noms de domaine que d'adresses IP.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1727" data-end=3D"1838" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"1729" data-end=3D"1838" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"1=
729" data-end=3D"1747">Centralisation</strong> : Les informations DNS peuve=
nt =C3=AAtre g=C3=A9r=C3=A9es =C3=A0 un point central, facilitant les chang=
ements.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1839" data-end=3D"1946" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"1841" data-end=3D"1946" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"1=
841" data-end=3D"1853">S=C3=A9curit=C3=A9</strong> : Le DNS peut =C3=AAtre =
configur=C3=A9 pour bloquer l'acc=C3=A8s =C3=A0 des sites non s=C3=A9curis=
=C3=A9s ou malveillants.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"1948" data-end=3D"1951" class=3D"">
<h2 data-start=3D"1953" data-end=3D"1984" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
1956" data-end=3D"1984">2. Types de Serveurs DNS</strong></h2>
<h3 data-start=3D"1986" data-end=3D"2016" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
1990" data-end=3D"2016">2.1. Serveur DNS Local</strong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"2017" data-end=3D"2330" class=3D"">Un serveur DNS local es=
t souvent utilis=C3=A9 dans les r=C3=A9seaux d'entreprise pour r=C3=A9soudr=
e les noms internes, tels que les serveurs de fichiers ou les imprimantes. =
Ce serveur peut =C3=AAtre configur=C3=A9 pour r=C3=A9soudre les noms intern=
es au r=C3=A9seau et =C3=A9galement interroger des serveurs DNS externes po=
ur r=C3=A9soudre les noms Internet.</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"2332" data-end=3D"2364" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
2336" data-end=3D"2364">2.2. Serveur DNS Externe</strong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"2365" data-end=3D"2606" class=3D"">Les serveurs DNS extern=
es sont utilis=C3=A9s pour r=C3=A9soudre les noms de domaines publics (comm=
e <strong data-start=3D"2455" data-end=3D"2473"><a data-start=3D"2457" data=
-end=3D"2471" rel=3D"noopener" target=3D"_new" class=3D"" href=3D"http://ww=
w.google.com/">www.google.com</a></strong>) et sont souvent fournis par vot=
re fournisseur d'acc=C3=A8s Internet (FAI) ou des entreprises tierces (par =
exemple, Google DNS, OpenDNS).</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"2608" data-end=3D"2640" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
2612" data-end=3D"2640">2.3. Serveur DNS Caching</strong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"2641" data-end=3D"2877" class=3D"">Les serveurs DNS locaux=
 stockent en cache les r=C3=A9sultats des requ=C3=AAtes pr=C3=A9c=C3=A9dent=
es pour r=C3=A9duire la charge r=C3=A9seau et am=C3=A9liorer les performanc=
es. Cela signifie que si un nom de domaine est d=C3=A9j=C3=A0 r=C3=A9solu, =
il peut =C3=AAtre r=C3=A9cup=C3=A9r=C3=A9 plus rapidement.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"2879" data-end=3D"2882" class=3D"">
<h2 data-start=3D"2884" data-end=3D"2932" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
2887" data-end=3D"2932">3. Configurer un Serveur DNS sous Windows</strong><=
/h2>
<p data-start=3D"2934" data-end=3D"3190" class=3D"">Dans un r=C3=A9seau Win=
dows, il existe plusieurs fa=C3=A7ons de configurer les param=C3=A8tres DNS=
, en fonction du type de r=C3=A9seau (LAN priv=C3=A9, r=C3=A9seau d'entrepr=
ise, etc.). Nous allons aborder comment configurer DNS =C3=A0 la fois sur u=
n client Windows et sur un serveur Windows.</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"3192" data-end=3D"3241" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
3196" data-end=3D"3241">3.1. Configurer DNS sur un Client Windows</strong><=
/h3>
<p data-start=3D"3243" data-end=3D"3325" class=3D"">Voici les =C3=A9tapes p=
our configurer un serveur DNS sous Windows sur un poste client :</p>
<h4 data-start=3D"3327" data-end=3D"3363" class=3D"">1. Ouvrir les Param=C3=
=A8tres R=C3=A9seau</h4>
<ul data-start=3D"3364" data-end=3D"3505">
<li data-start=3D"3364" data-end=3D"3439" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3366" data-end=3D"3439" class=3D"">Appuyez sur <code data-=
start=3D"3378" data-end=3D"3391">Windows + R</code>, tapez <strong data-sta=
rt=3D"3399" data-end=3D"3411">ncpa.cpl</strong>, puis appuyez sur <code dat=
a-start=3D"3430" data-end=3D"3438">Entr=C3=A9e</code>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3440" data-end=3D"3505" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3442" data-end=3D"3505" class=3D"">Cette action ouvre les =
<strong data-start=3D"3465" data-end=3D"3486">Connexions r=C3=A9seau</stron=
g> sur votre machine.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h4 data-start=3D"3507" data-end=3D"3553" class=3D"">2. Acc=C3=A9der aux Pr=
opri=C3=A9t=C3=A9s de la Connexion</h4>
<ul data-start=3D"3554" data-end=3D"3659">
<li data-start=3D"3554" data-end=3D"3659" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3556" data-end=3D"3659" class=3D"">Faites un <strong data-=
start=3D"3566" data-end=3D"3580">clic droit</strong> sur votre connexion r=
=C3=A9seau (Ethernet ou Wi-Fi) et s=C3=A9lectionnez <strong data-start=3D"3=
644" data-end=3D"3658">Propri=C3=A9t=C3=A9s</strong>.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h4 data-start=3D"3661" data-end=3D"3701" class=3D"">3. Modifier les Param=
=C3=A8tres TCP/IPv4</h4>
<ul data-start=3D"3702" data-end=3D"3854">
<li data-start=3D"3702" data-end=3D"3784" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3704" data-end=3D"3784" class=3D"">Cliquez sur <strong dat=
a-start=3D"3716" data-end=3D"3759">Protocole Internet Version 4 (TCP/IPv4)<=
/strong> puis sur <strong data-start=3D"3769" data-end=3D"3783">Propri=C3=
=A9t=C3=A9s</strong>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3785" data-end=3D"3854" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3787" data-end=3D"3854" class=3D"">Cochez l=E2=80=99option=
 <strong data-start=3D"3803" data-end=3D"3853">Utiliser les adresses de ser=
veur DNS suivantes</strong>.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h4 data-start=3D"3856" data-end=3D"3889" class=3D"">4. Configurer le Serve=
ur DNS</h4>
<ul data-start=3D"3890" data-end=3D"4189">
<li data-start=3D"3890" data-end=3D"4014" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3892" data-end=3D"4014" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"3=
892" data-end=3D"3915">Serveur DNS pr=C3=A9f=C3=A9r=C3=A9</strong> : Tapez =
l'adresse IP du serveur DNS de votre choix. Si vous utilisez Google DNS, en=
trez <code data-start=3D"4004" data-end=3D"4013">8.8.8.8</code>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4015" data-end=3D"4133" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4017" data-end=3D"4133" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"4=
017" data-end=3D"4043">Serveur DNS auxiliaire</strong> : Entrez une adresse=
 IP secondaire comme <code data-start=3D"4085" data-end=3D"4094">8.8.4.4</c=
ode> (Google DNS secondaire) si n=C3=A9cessaire.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4137" data-end=3D"4189" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4139" data-end=3D"4189" class=3D"">Cliquez sur <strong dat=
a-start=3D"4151" data-end=3D"4157">OK</strong> pour valider les modificatio=
ns.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h4 data-start=3D"4191" data-end=3D"4211" class=3D"">5. V=C3=A9rification</=
h4>
<ul data-start=3D"4212" data-end=3D"4399">
<li data-start=3D"4212" data-end=3D"4399" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4214" data-end=3D"4273" class=3D"">Ouvrez une fen=C3=AAtre=
