<h3 data-start=3D"5351" data-end=3D"5405" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
5355" data-end=3D"5403">Explication des informations suppl=C3=A9mentaires</=
strong> :</h3>
<ol data-start=3D"5406" data-end=3D"6237">
<li data-start=3D"5406" data-end=3D"5580" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"5409" data-end=3D"5580" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"5=
409" data-end=3D"5440">Description de l'adaptateur</strong> : Indique le mo=
d=C3=A8le de la carte r=C3=A9seau (par exemple, <strong data-start=3D"5494"=
 data-end=3D"5526">Intel(R) Ethernet Connection</strong> ou <strong data-st=
art=3D"5530" data-end=3D"5557">Qualcomm Atheros AR9485</strong> pour une ca=
rte Wi-Fi).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"5581" data-end=3D"5750" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"5584" data-end=3D"5750" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"5=
584" data-end=3D"5618">Adresse physique (MAC address)</strong> : Une adress=
e unique de l'adaptateur r=C3=A9seau, utilis=C3=A9e pour l'identification s=
ur le r=C3=A9seau local (par exemple, <code data-start=3D"5729" data-end=3D=
"5748">00-1A-2B-3C-4D-5E</code>).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"5751" data-end=3D"5856" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"5754" data-end=3D"5856" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"5=
754" data-end=3D"5788">Adresse IPv6 de liaison locale</strong> : Une adress=
e IPv6 g=C3=A9n=C3=A9r=C3=A9e automatiquement pour l'interface r=C3=A9seau.=
</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"5857" data-end=3D"6032" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"5860" data-end=3D"6032" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"5=
860" data-end=3D"5876">Serveurs DNS</strong> : Liste des serveurs DNS utili=
s=C3=A9s pour la r=C3=A9solution des noms de domaine (par exemple, <strong =
data-start=3D"5964" data-end=3D"5975">8.8.8.8</strong> et <strong data-star=
t=3D"5979" data-end=3D"5990">8.8.4.4</strong> sont les serveurs DNS publics=
 de Google).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6033" data-end=3D"6237" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"6036" data-end=3D"6237" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"6=
036" data-end=3D"6061">Carte r=C3=A9seau sans fil</strong> : Si vous avez p=
lusieurs cartes r=C3=A9seau, la commande <strong data-start=3D"6114" data-e=
nd=3D"6131">ipconfig /all</strong> vous montre les informations de toutes l=
es cartes actives, y compris les connexions sans fil et Ethernet.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<hr data-start=3D"6239" data-end=3D"6242" class=3D"">
<h2 data-start=3D"6244" data-end=3D"6289" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
6247" data-end=3D"6289">5. Options suppl=C3=A9mentaires de ipconfig</strong=
></h2>
<p data-start=3D"6291" data-end=3D"6459" class=3D"">La commande <strong dat=
a-start=3D"6303" data-end=3D"6315">ipconfig</strong> propose plusieurs opti=
