<p data-start=3D"2214" data-end=3D"2268" class=3D"">Voici une description d=
es options les plus courantes :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"2270" data-end=3D"2966">
<li data-start=3D"2270" data-end=3D"2333" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"2272" data-end=3D"2333" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"2=
272" data-end=3D"2283">netstat</strong> : Affiche la liste des connexions r=
=C3=A9seau actives.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2334" data-end=3D"2479" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"2336" data-end=3D"2479" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"2=
336" data-end=3D"2350">netstat -a</strong> : Affiche toutes les connexions =
et les ports d'=C3=A9coute (=C3=A0 la fois les connexions actives et les po=
rts ouverts sur votre machine).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2480" data-end=3D"2557" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"2482" data-end=3D"2557" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"2=
482" data-end=3D"2496">netstat -b</strong> : Affiche les programmes respons=
ables des connexions r=C3=A9seau.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2558" data-end=3D"2659" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"2560" data-end=3D"2659" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"2=
560" data-end=3D"2574">netstat -n</strong> : Affiche les adresses et num=C3=
=A9ros de port en format num=C3=A9rique (sans r=C3=A9solution DNS).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2660" data-end=3D"2733" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"2662" data-end=3D"2733" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"2=
662" data-end=3D"2676">netstat -o</strong> : Affiche l'ID du processus (PID=
) pour chaque connexion.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2734" data-end=3D"2819" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"2736" data-end=3D"2819" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"2=
736" data-end=3D"2750">netstat -s</strong> : Affiche les statistiques du r=
=C3=A9seau par protocole (TCP, UDP, etc.).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2820" data-end=3D"2870" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"2822" data-end=3D"2870" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"2=
822" data-end=3D"2836">netstat -r</strong> : Affiche la table de routage IP=
.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2871" data-end=3D"2966" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"2873" data-end=3D"2966" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"2=
873" data-end=3D"2898">netstat -p [protocol]</strong> : Affiche les connexi=
ons pour un protocole sp=C3=A9cifique (TCP ou UDP).</p>
</li>
</ul>
