<hr data-start=3D"1276" data-end=3D"1279" class=3D"">
<h2 data-start=3D"1281" data-end=3D"1348" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
1284" data-end=3D"1348">1. Introduction aux Services DNS et DHCP sous Windo=
ws Server</strong></h2>
<h3 data-start=3D"1350" data-end=3D"1385" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
1354" data-end=3D"1385">a. DNS (Domain Name System)</strong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"1386" data-end=3D"1675" class=3D"">Le <strong data-start=
=3D"1389" data-end=3D"1396">DNS</strong> est un service crucial pour la r=
=C3=A9solution des noms de domaine (par exemple, <code data-start=3D"1473" =
data-end=3D"1490">www.exemple.com</code>) en adresses IP utilisables par le=
s ordinateurs. Dans un environnement multi-sites, chaque site doit pouvoir =
r=C3=A9soudre les noms de domaine locaux et distants rapidement et efficace=
ment.</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"1677" data-end=3D"1730" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
1681" data-end=3D"1730">b. DHCP (Dynamic Host Configuration Protocol)</stro=
ng></h3>
<p data-start=3D"1731" data-end=3D"2059" class=3D"">Le <strong data-start=
=3D"1734" data-end=3D"1742">DHCP</strong> est utilis=C3=A9 pour attribuer a=
utomatiquement des adresses IP aux clients du r=C3=A9seau, facilitant la ge=
stion des adresses IP sans avoir besoin de les configurer manuellement. Dan=
s un environnement multi-sites, il est crucial que le DHCP soit configur=C3=
=A9 de mani=C3=A8re distribu=C3=A9e pour assurer la continuit=C3=A9 des ser=
vices r=C3=A9seau.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"2061" data-end=3D"2064" class=3D"">
<h2 data-start=3D"2066" data-end=3D"2117" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
2069" data-end=3D"2117">2. Configuration des Serveurs DNS Distribu=C3=A9s</=
strong></h2>
<h3 data-start=3D"2119" data-end=3D"2167" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
2123" data-end=3D"2167">a. Architecture du Serveur DNS Distribu=C3=A9</stro=
ng></h3>
<p data-start=3D"2168" data-end=3D"2499" class=3D"">Dans un environnement m=
ulti-sites, vous devez configurer un serveur DNS principal et plusieurs ser=
veurs DNS secondaires pour chaque site. Cela permet de r=C3=A9duire la char=
ge sur un seul serveur DNS et d=E2=80=99assurer que chaque site puisse r=C3=
=A9soudre les noms de domaine localement, tout en r=C3=A9pliquant les infor=
mations DNS entre les serveurs.</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"2501" data-end=3D"2556" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
2505" data-end=3D"2556">b. Installation et Configuration du Serveur DNS</st=
rong></h3>
<ol data-start=3D"2557" data-end=3D"3900">
<li data-start=3D"2557" data-end=3D"2772" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"2560" data-end=3D"2590" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"2=
560" data-end=3D"2588">Installation du r=C3=B4le DNS</strong> :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"2594" data-end=3D"2772">
<li data-start=3D"2594" data-end=3D"2690" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"2596" data-end=3D"2690" class=3D"">Ouvrez le <strong data-=
start=3D"2606" data-end=3D"2633">Gestionnaire de serveur</strong> et clique=
z sur <strong data-start=3D"2649" data-end=3D"2689">Ajouter des r=C3=B4les =
et fonctionnalit=C3=A9s</strong>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2694" data-end=3D"2772" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"2696" data-end=3D"2772" class=3D"">S=C3=A9lectionnez le r=
=C3=B4le <strong data-start=3D"2717" data-end=3D"2732">Serveur DNS</strong>=
 et suivez l=E2=80=99assistant pour l'installer.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2774" data-end=3D"3515" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"2777" data-end=3D"2920" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"2=
777" data-end=3D"2808">Configuration des Zones DNS</strong> :
Une fois le serveur DNS install=C3=A9, vous devez cr=C3=A9er les zones pour=
 g=C3=A9rer la r=C3=A9solution de noms de domaine :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"2928" data-end=3D"3194">
<li data-start=3D"2928" data-end=3D"3051" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"2930" data-end=3D"3051" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"2=
930" data-end=3D"2959">Zone de recherche directe</strong> : Cette zone cont=
ient les enregistrements qui r=C3=A9solvent les noms de domaine en adresses=
 IP.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3055" data-end=3D"3194" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3057" data-end=3D"3194" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"3=
057" data-end=3D"3086">Zone de recherche inverse</strong> : Cette zone perm=
et de r=C3=A9soudre les adresses IP en noms de domaine (utile pour la gesti=
on des reverse DNS).</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"3199" data-end=3D"3245" class=3D"">Pour cr=C3=A9er une <st=
rong data-start=3D"3214" data-end=3D"3243">zone de recherche directe</stron=
g> :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"3249" data-end=3D"3515">
<li data-start=3D"3249" data-end=3D"3357" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3251" data-end=3D"3357" class=3D"">Dans le <strong data-st=
art=3D"3259" data-end=3D"3279">Gestionnaire DNS</strong>, faites un clic dr=
oit sur <strong data-start=3D"3306" data-end=3D"3336">Zones de recherche di=
recte</strong> &gt; <strong data-start=3D"3339" data-end=3D"3356">Nouvelle =
zone</strong>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3361" data-end=3D"3511" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3363" data-end=3D"3511" class=3D"">S=C3=A9lectionnez <stro=
ng data-start=3D"3376" data-end=3D"3395">Zone principale</strong>, entrez l=
e nom de domaine, et choisissez l=E2=80=99option <strong data-start=3D"3446=
" data-end=3D"3461">Autoritaire</strong> ou <strong data-start=3D"3465" dat=
a-end=3D"3484">Non autoritaire</strong> selon votre configuration.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3516" data-end=3D"3900" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3519" data-end=3D"3722" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"3=
519" data-end=3D"3573">Configuration de la R=C3=A9plication entre Serveurs =
DNS</strong> :
Pour que les serveurs DNS soient synchronis=C3=A9s entre les sites, configu=
rez la <strong data-start=3D"3656" data-end=3D"3675">r=C3=A9plication DNS</=
strong> en mode <strong data-start=3D"3684" data-end=3D"3721">Active Direct=
ory-integrated zones</strong>.</p>
<ul data-start=3D"3726" data-end=3D"3900">
<li data-start=3D"3726" data-end=3D"3900" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3728" data-end=3D"3900" class=3D"">Dans <strong data-start=
=3D"3733" data-end=3D"3762">Propri=C3=A9t=C3=A9s de la zone DNS</strong>, s=
=C3=A9lectionnez <strong data-start=3D"3777" data-end=3D"3818">Stocker la z=
one dans Active Directory</strong> et choisissez la r=C3=A9plication au niv=
eau de <strong data-start=3D"3861" data-end=3D"3887">for=C3=AAt Active Dire=
ctory</strong> ou <strong data-start=3D"3891" data-end=3D"3899">site</stron=
g>.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ol>
<h3 data-start=3D"3902" data-end=3D"3952" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
3906" data-end=3D"3952">c. Configurer les Serveurs DNS Secondaires</strong>=
</h3>
<ol data-start=3D"3953" data-end=3D"4415">
<li data-start=3D"3953" data-end=3D"4240" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3956" data-end=3D"3995" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"3=
956" data-end=3D"3993">Ajouter un serveur DNS secondaire</strong> :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"3999" data-end=3D"4240">
<li data-start=3D"3999" data-end=3D"4144" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4001" data-end=3D"4144" class=3D"">Sur le serveur secondai=
re, ouvrez <strong data-start=3D"4035" data-end=3D"4055">Gestionnaire DNS</=
strong>, faites un clic droit sur <strong data-start=3D"4082" data-end=3D"4=
112">Zones de recherche directe</strong> &gt; <strong data-start=3D"4115" d=
ata-end=3D"4143">Nouvelle zone secondaire</strong>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4148" data-end=3D"4236" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4150" data-end=3D"4236" class=3D"">Entrez le nom de la zon=
e et sp=C3=A9cifiez le serveur DNS primaire (source de r=C3=A9plication).</=
p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4241" data-end=3D"4415" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4244" data-end=3D"4373" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"4=
244" data-end=3D"4278">V=C3=A9rification de la R=C3=A9plication</strong> :
Utilisez la commande <code data-start=3D"4305" data-end=3D"4315">nslookup</=
