=A9nements)</strong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"2428" data-end=3D"2650" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"2=
428" data-end=3D"2444">Event Viewer</strong> est un outil int=C3=A9gr=C3=A9=
 =C3=A0 Windows qui enregistre les =C3=A9v=C3=A9nements syst=C3=A8me et de =
s=C3=A9curit=C3=A9. Il peut =C3=AAtre utilis=C3=A9 pour surveiller des comp=
ortements suspects et g=C3=A9n=C3=A9rer des alertes en fonction des logs sp=
=C3=A9cifiques.</p>
<ol data-start=3D"2652" data-end=3D"3502">
<li data-start=3D"2652" data-end=3D"2898" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"2655" data-end=3D"2683" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"2=
655" data-end=3D"2681">Acc=C3=A9der =C3=A0 Event Viewer</strong> :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"2687" data-end=3D"2898">
<li data-start=3D"2687" data-end=3D"2767" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"2689" data-end=3D"2767" class=3D"">Ouvrez le menu <strong =
data-start=3D"2704" data-end=3D"2716">D=C3=A9marrer</strong>, tapez <strong=
 data-start=3D"2724" data-end=3D"2740">event viewer</strong> et appuyez sur=
 <strong data-start=3D"2756" data-end=3D"2766">Entr=C3=A9e</strong>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2771" data-end=3D"2898" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"2773" data-end=3D"2898" class=3D"">Acc=C3=A9dez =C3=A0 <st=
rong data-start=3D"2783" data-end=3D"2817">Applications and Services Logs</=
